MISDA PROJECT FILE STRUCTURE
================================================================================

1. CORE LIBRARY
---------------

misda/__init__.py
    Small public facade exporting the static MISDA API:
      - discover: structural inference and complete MIS universe.
      - evaluate: candidate-level linear, nonlinear, and Pareto evidence.
      - rank: ranking views under named policies.
      - benchmark: declaration-aware scientific assessment kept outside discovery.

misda/api.py
    Static discovery/evaluation/ranking implementation and typed result model:
      - MISSet and MISCandidate.
      - Ranking and the structural_coverage policy.
      - StructuralMetrics, LinearMetrics, NonlinearMetrics, and ParetoMetrics.
      - DimensionalSupport and CandidateSupport.

misda/_graph.py
    Construction of G+ and G±, independence-number dimensions, and structural
    MIS enumeration.

misda/_statistics.py
    Correlation statistics, alpha_onset/alpha_null estimation, empirical null
    envelope calibration, and aggressiveness interpolation.

misda/_support.py
    Data-driven dimensional-support diagnostics:
      - TRANSITIVE_CHAINING.
      - HIDDEN_SPECTRAL_STRUCTURE.

misda/_reconstruction.py
    Linear and nonlinear external reconstruction engines and nonlinear null
    reference protocol.

misda/_pareto.py
    Pareto-front preservation metrics.

misda/_ranking.py
    Structural candidate measurements used by ranking policies.

misda/_plotting.py
    Graph visualization for MISSet/Ranking objects.

misda/benchmark.py
    Benchmark declarations, reports, serialization, and regression comparison.

misda/benchmarks/
    Controlled diagnostic problem definitions, truth helpers, legacy regression
    generators, reproducible classical DTLZ references, and comparison helpers.

misda/benchmarks/validation.py
    Shared implementation for fixed-noise controlled validation, clean
    multi-sample robustness, and observation-noise robustness. Notebook and CLI
    front ends use this same implementation.


2. BENCHMARK NOTEBOOKS & FRONT ENDS (benchmarks/)
--------------------------------------------------

benchmarks/controlled.ipynb
    Canonical 13-case controlled benchmark under exact observation Y=Z, with
    one documented section per case and a final suite summary.

benchmarks/controlled_noisy.ipynb
    The same 13-case benchmark under a fixed scale-relative noisy observation
    regime, with per-case interpretation of what the added noise tests.

benchmarks/sampling_robustness.ipynb
    Clean sampling study across independent sample seeds with sigma=0,
    isolating finite-sample variability from observation noise.

benchmarks/noisy_robustness.ipynb
    Focused multi-sigma/multi-replicate observation-noise robustness study using
    a representative subset of controlled diagnostics.

benchmarks/comparison.ipynb
    MISDA/PCA method comparison on clean controlled diagnostics with explicit
    truth. Native estimands remain distinct; direct comparison uses a common
    external reconstruction score at explicitly named dimensions.

benchmarks/classical.ipynb
    MISDA on reproducible DTLZ2/DTLZ5 Pareto-front samples. Known front geometry
    is reference context, not MISDA latent/structural ground truth.

benchmarks/run_controlled.py
    Executable clean 13-problem scientific battery.

benchmarks/run_controlled_noisy.py
    Executable fixed-noise 13-problem reference battery.

benchmarks/run_sampling_robustness.py
    Executable clean multi-sample robustness study.

benchmarks/run_noisy_robustness.py
    Executable observation-noise robustness sweep.

benchmarks/run_comparison.py
    Executable diagnostic MISDA/PCA comparison battery.

benchmarks/run_classical.py
    Executable DTLZ2/DTLZ5 reference-MOP front end.

benchmarks/_baseline.py
    Historical baseline comparison helpers used only by regression tests.

benchmarks/cases.py
    Compatibility shim exposing the historical controlled generators used by
    characterization tests.

benchmarks/mop_definitions.py
    Compatibility shim for the historical MOP generator names.

benchmarks/r5_baseline.json
    Provenance marker for the successful pre-R5 acceptance artifacts.


